      <h3>Product Development Showcase</h3>
      <div>
        <figure class="shotset" style="margin-top:0"><div class="quad"><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Front three-quarter view of the Plasma Avatar concept scooter" width="722" height="520"></div><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Side view of the Plasma Avatar concept scooter" width="892" height="487"></div><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Rear view of the Plasma Avatar concept scooter" width="537" height="502"></div><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Top three-quarter view of the Plasma Avatar concept scooter" width="572" height="467"></div></div><figcaption><strong>Plasma Avatar (Concept)</strong><br>My contributions were the mechanical design of the chassis assembly and battery pack, and material selection for the body panels. The chassis is designed for pressure die casting in high-grade aluminium alloy A380, engineered for high strength at low weight to support higher cruising speeds for longer periods. The battery pack is structurally integrated into the frame, reducing part count and simplifying component integration and maintenance.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="shotset"><div class="five"><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Front three-quarter render of the hybrid throttle electric bicycle concept" width="607" height="522"></div><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Side view render of the hybrid throttle electric bicycle concept" width="800" height="492"></div><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Rear three-quarter render of the hybrid throttle electric bicycle concept" width="695" height="510"></div><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Top front three-quarter render of the hybrid throttle electric bicycle concept" width="766" height="547"></div><div class="shot"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Top rear three-quarter render of the hybrid throttle electric bicycle concept" width="742" height="562"></div></div><figcaption><strong>Hybrid Throttle Electric Bicycle (Concept)</strong><br>Spearheaded the entire design workflow from concept development to detailed designing, component and materials selection and assembly. The frame follows a vintage aesthetic design language of smooth, continuous curves, which reduces stress concentrations and improves structural fatigue life. A compact power train design simplifies installation and maintenance.</figcaption></figure>
